<title>USA: Coast Guard probes gasoline spill in Portland, ME..</title>
<headline>Coast Guard probes gasoline spill in Portland, ME..</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH PORTLAND, Maine 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>An estimated 20,000 gallons of gasoline spilled into Portland Harbor during a barge-loading accident, the Coast Guard said.</p>
<p>Investigators on Thursday were trying to determine what caused the spill, which happened when workers at the  Gulf Oil terminal were loading a barge owned by Boston Fuel Co on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The unleaded gasoline was destined for Bucksport.</p>
<p>No injuries were reported and environmental damage was expected to be limited because gasoline quickly evaporates, Coast Guard and environmental officials said.</p>
</text>
